// EXPECTED: compile error
// expect-error: string literal is read-only
// BUG-790 boundary. Making the global CONST form compile must not open the
// MUTABLE one: a string literal lives in .rodata, so binding it to a mutable
// global slice would let `NAME[0] = 65` write read-only memory (a SIGSEGV on
// hosted, a silent no-op or fault on bare metal).
//
// This also pins the DIAGNOSTIC. The generic path printed "cannot initialize
// 'NAME' of type '[]u8' with '[]u8'" — the same type on both sides, because
// type_name does not render the qualifier — which reads as a compiler bug rather
// than as the actionable "add const" it is.
[*]u8 NAME = "ZER";

u32 main() { return (u32)NAME.len; }
